Z||000003||mwbackus||03-24-2000||08:21 PM||||I have found that the IAC's can be a real pain to install and obtain a good airtight seal.  They also tend to loosen up after a while.  The only way I was able to get my latest one to seal was by using a very thin coat of silcone gasket sealant on both sides of the little round gasket that comes on the new valve.  I would also check for any vacuum leaks and/or a cracked EGR tube, since, a fluctuating vacuum leak can set a 35.<P>Mike<p>[This message has been edited by mwbackus (edited 03-24-2000).]||||reg||1
